      "writtenOn": "2022-11-07T17:17:01Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "What I mean is that I\u0027d prefer to just do black-box testing here. Ideally, the test wouldn\u0027t care how `charger_get_actual_current` is implemented, e.g. how many times it calls `get_actual_current` or with what arguments. In principle, changing the implementation to loop over every charger and then return the current for the specified one shouldn\u0027t break a test for the charger charger common code, even though that would be a bad change to make. \n\nObviously, a test with this architecture can\u0027t be completely ignorant of the implementation, because it has to provide a fake driver API implementation. And I don\u0027t think it\u0027s worth reorganizing the test to avoid doing that. But I still think it would be nice to minimize the amount of stuff this test checks that isn\u0027t guaranteed by the charger API.\n\nStill just a nit.",
